    "note": "Version read: introduced text as filed (2025-03-17). No votes recorded. Section 1 widens the definition by striking the sporting-purposes carve-out (old law removed) and adds feature-based categories. Appropriation amounts are blank. Exceptions in subd. 3 cover government and licensed-dealer transfers to law enforcement or armed forces."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 2 (Minn. Stat. 624.7145, subd. 1): As used in this section, \"transfer\" means a sale, gift, loan, assignment, or other delivery to another, whether or not for consideration.\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 624.7145, subd. 2): It is unlawful for a person to transfer a semiautomatic military-style assault weapon.\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 624.7145, subd. 4): A person who violates subdivision 2 is guilty of a felony and may be sentenced to imprisonment for not more than five years or to payment of a fine of not more than $25,000, or both.\nSection 3 (buyback program), subd. 1: The commissioner of public safety shall establish a statewide buyback program to purchase semiautomatic military-style assault weapons.\nSection 3 (buyback program), subd. 1: The program must accept any semiautomatic military-style assault weapon offered, regardless of the weapon's physical condition, and pay reimbursement at a rate set by the commissioner.\nSection 1 (Minn. Stat. 624.712, subd. 7): (6) conversion kit, part, or combination of parts from which an assault weapon can be assembled if those parts are in the possession or under the control of the same person."
